c'mon... "Why do you need p-values"? All science has been probability/p-value based for a long time and we are all used to it... so does this need any explanation? I don't want to only know if the beta is significantly different from zero, it's natural to know "how much significant" the beta is. p-value 0.001 or 0.02 or 0.06 actually makes a difference. Even in bayesian outputs I produce this probability and use the *** asterisk notattion to be able to quickly see result of the model...

